     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">The statistics dept. seminars can be abstruse, but this week’s looks like it may be worthwhile if you use splines. Details below.</p><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2\">Dr. Wang’s methods are implemented in the </span><a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/assist/index.html\" style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/assist/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468354155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EkyyR7NCe988N48m3kXey\">assist</a><span style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2\"> R package, for which an overview and manual are available </span><a href=\"http://www.pstat.ucsb.edu/faculty/yuedong/software.html\" style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.pstat.ucsb.edu/faculty/yuedong/software.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468354155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3KQsVFscXg1JBN0wCIsWJL\">on his website</a><span style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2\">.  I note that his </span><a href=\"http://www.pstat.ucsb.edu/faculty/yuedong/book/book.html\" style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.pstat.ucsb.edu/faculty/yuedong/book/book.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468354155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tcSeErPx6_eB5DFktf8pM\">book</a><span style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2\"> on these methods is available digitally </span><a href=\"http://harvest.lib.ucdavis.edu/F/?func=direct&amp;doc_number=003312537&amp;local_base=UCD01PUB\" style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://harvest.lib.ucdavis.edu/F/?func%3Ddirect%26doc_number%3D003312537%26local_base%3DUCD01PUB&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468354155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hccjzshdMlS3avVO-qZtg\">through the UCD library</a><span style=\"font-size:1em;line-height:1.2\">.</span></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:VGhlIHN0YXRpc3RpY3MgZGVwdC4gc2VtaW5hcnMgY2FuIGJlIGFic3RydXNlLCBidXQgdGhpcyB3\r\nZWVrJ3MgbG9va3MgbGlrZSBpdCBtYXkgYmUgd29ydGh3aGlsZSBpZiB5b3UgdXNlIHNwbGluZXMu\r\nIMKgRHIuIFdhbmcncyBtZXRob2RzIGFyZSBpbXBsZW1lbnRlZCBpbiB0aGUgW2Fzc2lzdF0oaHR0\r\ncDovL2NyYW4uci1wcm9qZWN0Lm9yZy93ZWIvcGFja2FnZXMvYXNzaXN0L2luZGV4Lmh0bWwpIFIg\r\ncGFja2FnZSwgZm9yIHdoaWNoIGFuIG92ZXJ2aWV3IGFuZCBtYW51YWwgYXJlIGF2YWlsYWJsZSBb\r\nb24gaGlzIHdlYnNpdGVdKGh0dHA6Ly93d3cucHN0YXQudWNzYi5lZHUvZmFjdWx0eS95dWVkb25n\r\nL3NvZnR3YXJlLmh0bWwpLiDCoEkgbm90ZSB0aGF0IGhpcyBbYm9va10oaHR0cDovL3d3dy5wc3Rh\r\ndC51Y3NiLmVkdS9mYWN1bHR5L3l1ZWRvbmcvYm9vay9ib29rLmh0bWwpIG9uIHRoZXNlIG1ldGhv\r\nZHMgaXMgYXZhaWxhYmxlIGRpZ2l0YWxseSBbdGhyb3VnaCB0aGUgVUNEIGxpYnJhcnldKGh0dHA6\r\nLy9oYXJ2ZXN0LmxpYi51Y2RhdmlzLmVkdS9GLz9mdW5jPWRpcmVjdCZhbXA7ZG9jX251bWJlcj0w\r\nMDMzMTI1MzcmYW1wO2xvY2FsX2Jhc2U9VUNEMDFQVUIpLjxzcGFuIHN0eWxlPSJmb250LXNpemU6\r\nIDEzLjE5OTk5OTgwOTI2NTFweDsiPiZuYnNwOzwvc3Bhbj4=\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div><span style=\"font-size:13.1999998092651px\"></span><span style=\"font-size:13.1999998092651px\"></span><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">---------- Forwarded message ---------<br>From: Pete Scully &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">psc...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;<br>Date: Tue, Mar 10, 2015 at 8:46 AM<br>Subject: STA 290 Seminar, Thur Mar 12: Yuedong Wang (UC Santa Barbara)<br>To: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stat-...@wald.ucdavis.edu</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stat-...@wald.ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;<br><br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You are invited to:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;color:#0070c0\">Statistics Seminar Series<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;padding:0in 0in 1.0pt 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thursday, March 12<sup>th</sup> 2015, 4:10pm, MSB 1147 (Colloquium Room)<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Refreshments at 3:30pm in MSB 4110 (Statistics Lounge)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Speaker:              <b>Yuedong Wang</b> (UC Santa Barbara)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in\">Title:                     \r\n<b>A Suite of S functions Implementing Spline smoothing Techniques</b><b><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in\">Abstract:              We present a suite of user friendly R functions for fitting various smoothing spline models including (a) non-parametric regression models for independent and correlated\r\n Gaussian data, and for independent binomial, Poisson and Gamma data;<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in\">(b) semi-parametric linear mixed-effects models;<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in\">(c) non-parametric nonlinear regression models;<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in\">(d) semi-parametric nonlinear regression models; and<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in\">(e) semi-parametric nonlinear mixed-effects models. The general form of smoothing splines based on reproducing kernel Hilbert spaces is used to model non-parametric functions. Thus these R functions deal with many\r\n different situations in a unified fashion. Well known special cases are polynomial, periodic, spherical, thin-plate and L splines, GAM, SS ANOVA, projection pursuit, multiple index, varying coefficient, functional linear and self-modeling nonlinear regression\r\n models.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-autospace:none\"><span lang=\"EN\">This abstract is also posted on our website at:\r\n<a href=\"http://www.stat.ucdavis.edu/seminars/winter15/031215-wang.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.stat.ucdavis.edu/seminars/winter15/031215-wang.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468354155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20qgoIApgdSJzgZyQ-AyG1\">http://www.stat.ucdavis.edu/seminars/winter15/031215-wang.html</a>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:12.0pt;margin-left:1.0in\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p><u></u><span style=\"font-family:Symbol\"><span>·<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">        \r\n</span></span></span><u></u><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div></div></div>\r\n"
